# NestJS Development Standards

When working in backend services (`auth-service`, `product-service`, `user-data-service`):

## Code Structure

- Follow the standard NestJS module pattern: `module -> controller -> service`.
- For Auth and Product services, use the local `src/prisma/PrismaService`.
- Use `class-validator` and `class-transformer` for request validation.

## Testing

- Use Vitest.
- Unit tests: `*.spec.ts` colocated with source.
- E2E/integration tests: `*.e2e-spec.ts` in each app's `test` folder.
- Base config: `@repo/vitest-config/nestjs`, extended in `apps/<service-name>/vitest.config.ts`.
- Keep unit and E2E coverage complementary (minimal overlap).

## Documentation

- For every new controller or public API, add `@ApiTags`, `@ApiOperation`, and `@ApiResponse` from `@nestjs/swagger`.

## Database

- Auth and Product use PostgreSQL, one schema per service (`app_auth`, `app_product`).
- Prisma schemas live in `apps/<service-name>/prisma/schema.prisma`.
- After schema changes, remind user to run `yarn workspace <service-name> generate`.
- MongoDB is used for the User Data Service only.
